-- Financial Statements — the authoritative reporting input (roadmap increment 11, foundation).
--
-- fs_reporting_input(company, year) is the ONE read the financial-statements workspace uses for figures:
--   (Adjustments: exactly those that APPLY to each certification — approved against it, or explicitly revalidated to
--   it after a re-check; one shared definition, _cr_adjustment_applies_to.)
--   current      the AUTHORITATIVE certification of the year (get_authoritative_certification — read-time authority,
--                staleness and invalidation included) with the approved adjustments bound to it applied as a layer
--                (close_review_adjusted_trial_balance), per account, in exact minor units, with the account's reviewed
--                placement (account_mappings) and its lineage: the certification, the upload, and every approved
--                adjustment that touched it;
--   comparative  the year before AS REPORTED: its authoritative certification with its own approved adjustments, or the
--                exact reason it is missing — a non-authoritative upload is never substituted;
--   adjustments  every approved adjustment applied, with whether it was self-approved (disclosure);
--   findings     the Close Review findings summary (unresolved blocking findings block Reviewed/Final, I8);
--   inputSha256  SHA-256 of the canonical identity of all of the above (certifications, adjustments, findings run):
--                a saved report records it; when it changes the report is stale.
-- Nothing here writes. Readable by members with workspace access while the financial-statements rollout allows the
-- company. No tax engine output is read (revision 5 §1.5).
--
